WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.235
- On this episode, we bring
the ruckus on floor 15.

00:00:16.344 --> 00:00:20.726
- [Gary] You ask questions,
and I answer them.

00:00:21.783 --> 00:00:26.627
This is The #AskGaryVee Show.

00:00:30.127 --> 00:00:32.009
Hello, everybody. This is episode 146

00:00:32.009 --> 00:00:34.650
of The #AskGaryVee Show. Sorry, guys.

00:00:34.650 --> 00:00:39.099
I'm on floor 15, I feel like we woke up

00:00:39.099 --> 00:00:41.107
the floor a little bit, feels nice.

00:00:41.107 --> 00:00:45.813
India, let's get into the show.

00:00:45.813 --> 00:00:47.737
- I'm not gonna try anymore.

00:00:47.737 --> 00:00:48.734
- Is that true?

00:00:48.734 --> 00:00:49.938
- [India] No.
- You've given up?

00:00:49.938 --> 00:00:51.531
- [India] No.
- Okay, got it.

00:00:51.531 --> 00:00:54.354
- [Voiceover] Aaron asks, "You
mention how great you are

00:00:54.354 --> 00:00:57.033
"at closing and sales. What's
your structure for your pitches?"

00:00:58.143 --> 00:01:00.796
- For my pitches. So, my
structure for my pitches is

00:01:00.796 --> 00:01:02.678
complete and utter no structure.

00:01:02.678 --> 00:01:05.547
I don't really structure
my pitches a whole lot.

00:01:05.547 --> 00:01:08.395
My team may, in certain
scenarios, have a deck.

00:01:08.395 --> 00:01:10.414
But there's, I'm sure, an
inside joke in this company

00:01:10.414 --> 00:01:12.552
that when we go into that
meeting, I'm gonna completely

00:01:12.552 --> 00:01:16.260
side-rail and drive over that
deck, which I do consistently.

00:01:16.260 --> 00:01:18.677
I'm much more interested
in reading the room

00:01:18.677 --> 00:01:23.227
and deploying what that client
wants at that exact moment,

00:01:23.227 --> 00:01:25.879
versus what we thought they wanted.

00:01:25.879 --> 00:01:28.316
In the same way I sold
at baseball card shows,

00:01:28.316 --> 00:01:31.078
I would just always react.
I really think my pitches

00:01:31.078 --> 00:01:32.913
are structured for counter-punching.

00:01:32.913 --> 00:01:36.145
Which means no preparation
from presentation form,

00:01:36.145 --> 00:01:40.511
but complete and utter presentation
for knowing the content.

00:01:40.511 --> 00:01:42.245
See what I mean? This is
the thing that most people

00:01:42.245 --> 00:01:45.382
don't understand. They
think that you wing it.

00:01:45.382 --> 00:01:48.154
No, you're winging the way
you're gonna present it.

00:01:48.154 --> 00:01:51.501
You're not winging what
you actually know about it.

00:01:51.501 --> 00:01:55.749
So the way I prepare,
is holistically prepare.

00:01:55.749 --> 00:01:58.789
A.K.A. know my shit. I
know what I'm talking about

00:01:58.789 --> 00:02:00.067
in the things that I'm selling.

00:02:00.067 --> 00:02:02.352
And then basically I'm
reverse engineering deploying

00:02:02.352 --> 00:02:06.022
your needs against that
expertise at that moment,

00:02:06.022 --> 00:02:09.532
versus what order the deck
needs to be in the presentation.

00:02:09.532 --> 00:02:10.975
My friends, the deck doesn't sell it.

00:02:10.975 --> 00:02:14.920
The presentation doesn't
sell it. The skills sell it.

00:02:14.920 --> 00:02:17.447
- [Voiceover] Jeremy asks,
"Gary, why do you feel the need

00:02:17.447 --> 00:02:20.405
"to swear to make a point?
Surely business credibility

00:02:20.405 --> 00:02:23.357
"is better built without swearing?

00:02:23.357 --> 00:02:25.857
- You were excited about
asking this question?

00:02:25.857 --> 00:02:28.624
I don't feel like I need
to swear to make a point.

00:02:28.624 --> 00:02:31.822
I also don't agree that
business credibility

00:02:31.822 --> 00:02:34.803
is lost when you curse. Business
credibility is lost when

00:02:34.803 --> 00:02:38.365
you curse when the judge
of your credibility

00:02:38.365 --> 00:02:40.943
is a d or f player and
somebody that is making

00:02:40.943 --> 00:02:44.287
surface level decisions. As a
matter of fact, I would argue that,

00:02:44.287 --> 00:02:47.733
at times, I use my cursing
as a filter to filter out

00:02:47.733 --> 00:02:49.928
the people that are not capable of

00:02:49.928 --> 00:02:52.991
seeing the bigger picture,
versus being so blocked.

00:02:52.991 --> 00:02:54.867
"Oh my god. I heard the word (bleep).

00:02:54.867 --> 00:02:57.738
I can't hear anything else.
Everything else must be bad.

00:02:57.738 --> 00:02:59.878
There's no good advice,
this is a bad person."

00:02:59.878 --> 00:03:02.424
That is ludicrous. It
goes into the same context

00:03:02.424 --> 00:03:05.383
as the way you dress, or
a million other variables

00:03:05.383 --> 00:03:07.204
of ways people that will judge you--

00:03:07.204 --> 00:03:12.204
See, when you're great, you
can dress in all red, all red.

00:03:12.707 --> 00:03:15.751
You can blend into phone booths.

00:03:15.751 --> 00:03:18.468
I mean, you can dress how you want.

00:03:18.468 --> 00:03:21.760
You can talk how you want.
Because at the end of the day,

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:25.326
the way you deliver is all
that people really care about.

00:03:25.326 --> 00:03:27.101
And the way you make them feel.

00:03:27.101 --> 00:03:29.304
I'm not cursing to disrespect someone.

00:03:29.304 --> 00:03:31.523
I have empathy and respect
why a lot of people

00:03:31.523 --> 00:03:33.501
may not like me, or consume me.

00:03:33.501 --> 00:03:35.274
There are plenty of people
that don't watch this video

00:03:35.274 --> 00:03:37.757
because they saw a keynote where I cursed

00:03:37.757 --> 00:03:39.707
and they were offended, and
they are no longer in my set.

00:03:39.707 --> 00:03:42.688
Surely, I would have a bigger
audience if I didn't curse.

00:03:42.688 --> 00:03:45.518
That is absolutely true.
And business respect, sure.

00:03:45.518 --> 00:03:49.064
I may lose out on a deal
because they were offended.

00:03:49.064 --> 00:03:52.871
But in the net, net, net
score, I win so many more

00:03:52.871 --> 00:03:57.683
by being me and just being me
versus creating a half-version

00:03:57.683 --> 00:04:00.781
of me for the one conservative
person and leaving

00:04:00.781 --> 00:04:03.245
the hundreds of magic
business opportunities,

00:04:03.245 --> 00:04:05.068
that are predicated on
winners making decisions.

00:04:05.068 --> 00:04:09.284
So, yeah. I'm completely
in disagreement with you.

00:04:09.284 --> 00:04:13.223
I don't believe either one of us

00:04:13.223 --> 00:04:14.803
